  "label": "intended audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed for an audience that understands and finds humor in antisemitic stereotypes, particularly those referencing the Holocaust and dehumanizing metaphors. The target community includes individuals who may be exposed to or propagate hate speech, and who are likely to engage with or share content that mocks Jewish people using historical trauma as a punchline. The meme relies on cultural knowledge of the Holocaust and antisemitic tropes to create its offensive impact, so the intended audience is one that either has prior exposure to these themes or is willing to consume and disseminate hateful content without recognizing its harmful nature.",
